Dumi: I'm not going to ask you what happened to it.
Dumi: I don't need to know. I'd rather not know, honestly.
Dumi: What I need is for it to be replaced by the end of the month, and for you to be the one who tells people it was you who replaced it.
Dumi: Then come and say so, to me, before the end of the month. Not after.
Dumi: You're welcome here either way. That isn't in question and I want you to hear that clearly.
Dumi: My father would have known how to do that better.
